      {"uuid": "b1", "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-09-10T18:00:00Z", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Why do bond prices fall when interest rates rise?"}]},
      {"uuid": "b2", "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-09-10T18:00:05Z", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Think of it like an old phone: when a better model comes out, yours is worth less. For example, a 3% bond looks worse once new bonds pay 5%."}]},
      {"uuid": "b3", "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-09-10T18:01:00Z", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "So the old bond pays less than new ones, so people pay less for it?"}]},
      {"uuid": "b4", "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-09-10T18:01:05Z", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Right."}]}
    ]
  },
